      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The greatest advantage of the baboon model is the phylogenetic closeness of the animal to man which may be of considerable importance when dealing with receptor-related events and with drug-specific therapy. The major disadvantage is the difficulty of dealing with awake baboons and the absence of any adequate model for coronary artery spasm."},
